{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Investigation evidence (origin/main 4b74c52b378)\n\n**Gating cell selection, verbatim from `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`, job `test`.** The `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` cell runs TWO pytest steps, in order:\n\n1. Step `Run the default suite (Python tiers; excludes integration + external)` (line 743):\n   `DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS: ${{ matrix.os == 'macos-latest' && 'platform_compat and not external' || (matrix.python-version == '3.13' && 'not integration and not external' || 'not integration and not external and not repo_policy') }}`\n   run: `pytest -m \"$DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS\" -n 4 --dist worksteal ...` -> resolves to `not integration and not external` for this cell.\n2. Step `Run the integration tier (concurrency + reconciler; network-guarded)` (line 817):\n   run: `pytest -m integration -n 4 --dist loadgroup --max-worker-restart=0 -q -p no:cacheprovider --durations=25 --basetemp=...`\n\nEvery matrix cell runs step 2. `make test` (Makefile line 587) runs only step 1's selection: `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n $(PYTEST_WORKERS) --dist worksteal -q`.\n\n**Mechanism of the miss.** `tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability.py` (renamed from `..._heldout.py` by 4b74c52b378) sets `pytestmark = pytest.mark.integration`, so only step 2 selects it. In run 41271076673 all 4 cells passed step 1 and failed step 2 (ubuntu py3.13: step 1 03:58:59-04:22:40Z, step 2 04:22:41-04:24:47Z failure).\n\n**Why the parity tests missed it.** `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_repo_policy_nodes_run_only_in_the_existing_primary_cell` pins the CI side only: it compares DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS to a hard-coded constant `_DEFAULT_SELECTION = \"not integration and not external\"` and asserts the integration step exists. No test reads the Makefile `test` recipe, and no test treats the gating cell as the union of its pytest steps. `tests/unit/test_verify_gate_parity.py` covers the Gerrit vote job's `needs`, not selection. So the Makefile could (and did) omit step 2 with every parity test green.\n\n**Prior intent.** Bug 1035-bed7-c855-4732 (closed) created `make verify` with the stated resolution \"complete BY CONSTRUCTION -- make test already carries exactly CI's DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS ... nothing is enumerated and nothing can drift\". It equated the gating cell with step 1 alone; nothing in that ticket or its comments discusses the integration step or decides to exclude it. The `-m \"not integration and not external\"` string in `make test` dates from b288e7037e4 (2026-06-24), before `make verify` existed. The stated intent is parity with the gating cell, so the fix restores parity rather than changing the docs.\n\n**Cost of the corrected selection (measured on this host, -n 4).** `pytest --collect-only -m integration`: 200 tests (vs 20,221 in the default tier). Full integration-tier run with CI's flags: 196 passed, 4 skipped, 219 s pytest / 222 s wall (one test, `test_import_batch_resume.py::test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass`, is 89 s of it). On CI the step took 2-4 min per cell. Adds roughly 4 min to `make verify`'s measured 22-26 min."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793532635812635001,"uuid":"0d08743f-42c1-43cc-ace1-adf7f3dbb7f6"}